# Clean URLs for data-driven pages. One HTML file serves every section and book.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. Cloudflare matches these top to bottom and stops at the first
# hit, so every specific rule has to sit above the splat that would swallow it.
# The renames were below /s/* and never fired — the build log flagged it.

# Knowledge became Maps and Education became Library. 301 rather than a
# rewrite: the old slug is genuinely gone, and a rewrite would leave two URLs
# serving one section forever, which is how stale links never get fixed.
/s/knowledge    /s/maps            301
/s/knowledge/*  /s/maps/:splat     301
/s/education    /s/library         301
/s/education/*  /s/library/:splat  301

# Destinations carry .html explicitly. The extensionless form relied on Pages
# normalising /section to section.html, which is not something to depend on —
# a destination that fails to resolve does not error, it falls through to the
# root index, so every section link silently renders the home page.
/s        /section.html   200
/s/*      /section.html   200
/read     /reader.html    200
/read/*   /reader.html    200
